A string whose plain form would reload as something else — an alias, an anchor, a tag, a
mapping, or padded text — is written single-quoted so it reloads as the text it was given.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md 'a=@lead' 'b=*star' 'c=&anchor' 'd=!bang' 'e=%pct' 'f=`tick' 'h= padded ' 'g=a: b'
-- exit --
0
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: a=@lead, b=*star, c=&anchor, d=!bang, e=%pct, f=`tick, h= padded , g=a: b
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
a: '@lead'
b: '*star'
c: '&anchor'
d: '!bang'
e: '%pct'
f: '`tick'
h: ' padded '
g: 'a: b'
---
# Body
